What prints, and in what order?

```js
console.log("A");
setTimeout(() => console.log("B"), 0);
console.log("C");
```

In this nested timer example, why must `4` print before `2`?

```js
console.log(1);
setTimeout(() => {
  console.log(2);
  setTimeout(() => console.log(3), 0);
}, 0);
console.log(4);
```
